    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-ceiling leadoff hitters who project as our most reliable assets. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) earns the top spot on the board against Michael McGreevy, benefiting from a favorable 13% dynamic platoon boost and the inherent value of his top-of-the-order positioning. Close behind, **Gunnar Henderson** (73.30) is a must-start despite facing a lefty in Jacob Lopez; the massive 16% park factor and 10% order premium outweigh the platoon tax, signaling an aggressive play for power and runs. **Coby Mayo** (63.97) also presents an intriguing value, as his profile gains significant lift from the park factor, keeping him viable despite the lower lineup slotting. \n\nWhile **Sam Antonacci** (60.82) cracks our primary starting group due to a strong xwOBA of .398, the most difficult choice involved the benching of **Miguel Vargas** (51.54). **Miguel Vargas** was the closest exclusion, as his proximity to **Marcell Ozuna**\u2019s (51.56) score shows how thin the margin is between our final UTIL spot and the pine; ultimately, the optimizer favored **Marcell Ozuna**\u2019s stability, as **Miguel Vargas** faced potential drag from negative park factors and minor SB-related efficiency concerns. We are currently navigating a \"Lineup Pending\" environment across the board, which introduces significant volatility. Specifically, **Kyle Tucker** (52.24) faces the stiffest test of the day against Chris Sale; while his elite talent keeps him in the lineup, we must monitor for any late-breaking weather or lineup adjustments that could further depress his efficiency against such a high-tier arm.",
